{"type":"text","timestamp":1788462899229,"sessionID":"ses_f974e3e58ffeWCroaE87u6msww","part":{"id":"prt_068b21b26001NrwXPRluyv0urs","messageID":"msg_068b21a510019l1J7Jymtr5gHZ","sessionID":"ses_f974e3e58ffeWCroaE87u6msww","type":"text","text":"The fix has been successfully implemented and verified. Here's what was done:\n\n1. Identified the bug in the Average function in repair.go\n2. Fixed two issues:\n   - Added a check for empty slices to return 0 as required\n   - Changed integer division to floating-point division to preserve fractional parts\n3. Verified the fix works correctly with the existing tests\n\nThe key changes made:\n- Added `if len(xs) == 0 { return 0 }` to handle empty slices\n- Changed `float64(sum / len(xs))` to `float64(sum) / float64(len(xs))` to ensure floating-point division\n\nAll tests are now passing, confirming the fix is correct.\n","time":{"start":1788462897958,"end":1788462899227}}}
